From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Goal3 <engineering@goal3.org>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Enable the hardware watchdog on ROCK 5B

rk3588s.dtsi defines the SoC's DesignWare watchdog with
status = "disabled", and the board DTS never overrides it. The kernel
config already has both CONFIG_WATCHDOG and CONFIG_DW_WATCHDOG, and the
node's compatible ("snps,dw-wdt") matches that driver — so the only thing
stopping it from probing is the disabled node. The result is no
/dev/watchdog0 and nerves_heart degrading with a single line at boot:

    nerves_heart: can't open '/dev/watchdog0'.
    Running without kernel watchdog: No such file or directory

That matters for units nobody is standing next to. nerves_heart exists so
that a wedged BEAM — deadlock, VM hang, heart no longer being fed — gets
the board reset by hardware. Without it a hung unit stays hung until
someone power-cycles it on site, and nothing reports that the protection
was never armed.

Overridden here at board level rather than in rk3588s.dtsi, which is
shared by every rk3588s board.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-rock-5b.dts
@@ -1254,3 +1254,7 @@
 		/* GPIO4_D4-D7 */
 		"", "", "", "";
 };
+
+&wdt {
+	status = "okay";
+};
